# GS Director: pass the device UDID

Whenever Paul asks to **fix, change, or finish** GS Director (`mobile/apps/gsDirector`), treat verification as part of the work — not an optional follow-up.

## Device

- Do **not** hard-code a simulator or hardware UDID in scripts, YAML, docs defaults, or Cursor rules.
- Paul names the target for the run. Pass it as `DIRECTOR_DEVICE_UDID` (or `node scripts/run-maestro.js --device <udid>`). Fail if it is missing.
- Maestro YAML must not name a device; the runner supplies `--device` so the same flows can hit different iPads.
- Do not boot or shut down simulators. Target an already-running instance. Maestro: `--shutdown-after=false`.
- Do not use the 2018 A12X unless Paul named it or the task is thermal measurement.

## How much testing

After the code change, run **as much of the suite that already exists** as the change can affect:

1. `DIRECTOR_DEVICE_UDID=<udid> ./scripts/build-sim.sh` (simulator) or `build-device.sh` (hardware) so Maestro `clearState` has an `.app`
2. `DIRECTOR_DEVICE_UDID=<udid> ./scripts/test-unit.sh` when Swift logic changed
3. `node scripts/run-maestro.js --device <udid> --suite operator` for product/UI/pipeline work

Quote the runner line that names the UDID. Fix failures before handing back.

Thermals on the A12X stay a separate series (Peltier rule).
